<title>GERMANY: German building union to demand full sick pay.</title>
<headline>German building union to demand full sick pay.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's IG-Bau construction sector trade union said on Thursday it would seek the continuation of full sick pay entitlement when it meets employers next week.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be demanding 100 percent sick pay. We shall seek to have it included in a sensible package,&quot; IG-Bau chairman Klaus Wiesehuegel told a news briefing.</p>
<p>He added the union was not however planning to discuss its wider 1997 wage claim in the discussions set for Wednesday.</p>
<p>IG-Bau has until now stayed largely out of a bitter dispute between employers and trade unions over a law passed in October allowing companies to cut workers' sick pay from the current 100 percent of salary to 80 percent.</p>
